These prompts change the ONCE Go CLI/TUI in this repository, one feature per file, run in order with a fresh agent for each.

House style here is the project's own Go conventions plus `make lint`; the wider reference copy is at /home/mrjohn/Work/tries/2026-11-03-house-style/house-style

The last line of every file is the same, and it means `make test` and `make lint` both run clean.

Each file is the whole instruction for its session. Read only the one you are running.
===
Your job is to go in and inject a bar into every page ONCE serves here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Forty pixels tall, the app name on the left, then back, next, contents, drift, reload and hide. Dark glass over whatever the page is, and the page itself is never modified on disk.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

/home/mrjohn/Work/tries/2026-11-03-house-style/house-style
===
Your job is to go in and add Drift here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

`R` opens a random running app, never the one you are already on. No settings and no history, it just picks.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

